cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: PolyUQ
abstract: >-
  Polymorphic Uncertainty Quantification for Operational Modal Analysis.
  Propagates mixed aleatory/epistemic uncertainty — random variables,
  intervals, and Dempster-Shafer evidence — through arbitrary mapping
  functions, and post-processes results into imprecision (belief /
  plausibility) and incompleteness bounds. The methodology was developed
  from 2022 within the oma_uq research repository; see CHANGELOG.md for
  development history.
authors:
  - family-names: Marwitz
    given-names: Simon
  - family-names: Zabel
    given-names: Volkmar
version: 0.1.0a1
date-released: "2026-07-08"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/simonmarwitz/PolyUQ"
url: "https://github.com/simonmarwitz/PolyUQ"
keywords:
  - uncertainty quantification
  - imprecise probabilities
  - Dempster-Shafer
  - evidence theory
  - operational modal analysis
  - structural health monitoring
